      "text": "Your grandma says “vos”. What does it mean?"
    },
    {
      "path": "app/grammar-classroom/live/lessons/g239.ts",
      "text": "Spanish has 27 letters. Good news: it almost always sounds the way it is written. If you can see the word, you can say it."
    },
    {
      "path": "app/grammar-classroom/live/lessons/g239.ts",
      "text": "The five vowels always sound the same: a (ah), e (eh), i (ee), o (oh), u (oo). Short and clear. That is why “abuela” is easy: a-bue-la."
    },
    {
      "path": "app/grammar-classroom/live/lessons/g239.ts",
      "text": "Your grandparents will ask how your name is spelt. Spell it with the letter names: “Alex: a, ele, e, equis”."
    },
    {
      "path": "app/grammar-classroom/live/lessons/g239.ts",
      "text": "How does the “h” in “hola” sound?"
    },
    {
      "path": "app/grammar-classroom/live/lessons/g239.ts",
      "text": "How many vowels does “abuela” have?"
    },
    {
      "path": "app/grammar-classroom/live/lessons/g239.ts",
      "text": "What is the letter “ñ” called?"
    },
    {
      "path": "app/grammar-classroom/live/lessons/g239.ts",
      "text": "“Vos” and “bos” sound…"
    },
