    },
    {
      "path": "app/grammar-classroom/live/lessons/g239.ts",
      "text": "mate (the drink)"
    },
    {
      "path": "app/grammar-classroom/live/lessons/g239.ts",
      "text": "grandma"
    },
    {
      "path": "app/grammar-classroom/live/lessons/g239.ts",
      "text": "To speak, we first say who: I, you, he, she… These are the pronouns. Today you need three: yo (I), tú / vos (you), and the rest only to recognise them."
    },
    {
      "path": "app/grammar-classroom/live/lessons/g239.ts",
      "text": "“Soy Alex” and “Yo soy Alex” are the same. The verb already says who is speaking. At the start, say the pronoun if it helps you."
    },
    {
      "path": "app/grammar-classroom/live/lessons/g239.ts",
      "text": "Tú and vos are the same person: “you”. With vos the verb changes a little: tú eres → vos sos. Today you only need to recognise it when your grandparents say it."
    },
    {
      "path": "app/grammar-classroom/live/lessons/g239.ts",
      "text": "Your grandma talks about herself. Which pronoun does she use?"
